{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '254,381p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; sed -n '235,330p;690,720p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; cat host/gambit/yin/dao/posix/file.jolt; rg -n 'jolt-file|java.io.File|\\\"exists\\\"|\\\"isDirectory\\\"' host/chez\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- node-over\n  \"The node composed from checked `opts` over the opened `local` store.\"\n  [opts local]\n  (let [{:keys [peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes bind!]}\n        opts\n        [requests answers facts ticks traffic ledger] (repeatedly 6 ring)\n        socket? (boolean (seq peers))\n        ;; The effective transport configuration, resolved once here and\n        ;; used consistently by every consumer of it: the DHT state, the\n        ;; store front's own oversize refusal, and the payload capability\n        ;; a storage composition declares (`payload-budget`).  Three\n        ;; consumers reading three defaults is how a bound and a budget\n        ;; come to disagree.\n        message-bound (or (::dht/max-message-bytes opts)\n                          (::dht/max-message-bytes dht/defaults))\n        composition (cond-> {:local local\n                             :requests requests\n                             :answers answers\n                             :facts facts\n                             :ticks ticks\n                             ::dht/id (dht/bytes->hex\n                                        (secure-random-bytes dht/id-length))\n                             ::dht/publish? publish?\n                             ::dht/bootstrap (vec peers)\n                             ::dht/bind-host bind-host}\n                      socket? (assoc :traffic traffic\n                                     ::dht/secret (secure-random-bytes\n                                                    secret-length)\n                                     ::dht/max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes))\n        seam (when socket?\n               (bind! {:identity (str \"dao.space.dht:\"\n                                      (subs (::dht/id composition) 0 16))\n                       :deposit traffic\n                       :bind-host bind-host\n                       :bind-port bind-port\n                       :max-bytes (::dht/max-datagram dht/defaults)}))\n        ;; the DHT handle's put checks (address, oversize) over :local; its\n        ;; own replicate request goes to a sink, since the node's step\n        ;; owns every request (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 5.5)\n        front (dht/store-handle\n                {:local local\n                 :requests (ring 1)\n                 :max-message-bytes message-bound})\n        closed? (volatile! false)]\n    {:peers (vec peers)\n     :publish? publish?\n     :message-bound message-bound\n     :limits (select-keys opts [:max-backlog :repair-batch :max-open\n                                :repair-slots :repair-ticks :repair-max-ticks\n                                :max-repairing])\n     :composition composition\n     :dht (when-not socket? (dht/state composition))\n     :seam seam\n     :traffic-cursor (when socket? (oldest traffic))\n     :facts (oldest facts)\n     :ledger ledger\n     :ledger-cursor (oldest ledger)\n     :origin nil\n     :reading nil\n     :window (new-ledger)\n     :window-lost? false\n     :pubs []\n     :next-id 0\n     :fresh []\n     :repair []\n     :queued {}\n     :repair-owner {}\n     :inflight {}\n     :misses {}\n     :client (content.step/client-state requests answers (oldest answers))\n     :loads {}\n     :refusal nil\n     :handle {:put-bytes-fn (fn [address bs]\n                              (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn front) address bs)]\n                                (stream/append! ledger {::put address})\n                                verdict))\n              :get-bytes-fn (:get-bytes-fn local)\n              :close-fn (fn []\n                          (when-not @closed?\n                            (vreset! closed? true)\n                            (try (when seam ((:close! seam)))\n                                 (finally\n                                   (jing/close! local)))))}}))\n\n\n(defn join\n  \"Join the DHT from `opts` and answer the node:\n\n   * `:local`: the node's own `dao.jing` store, already opened (and, if\n     it is a directory, already locked) by the caller, as `yin.repl` does;\n     or `:dir`, a directory `join` opens as the durable directory store\n     (`dao.space.store/open`): exclusively, under the directory lock, so\n     a second owner in this process or another is refused naming it, and\n     the lock is held until `close!`;\n   * `:peers`: bootstrap contacts `[{:host ip :port p} ...]`, none for\n     solo;\n   * `:publish?`: whether everything in the local store is public;\n   * `:bind-host`, `:bind-port`: the socket's address, loopback and\n     ephemeral by default;\n   * `:max-inbound-bytes`: the inbound storage bound;\n   * `:bind!`: the datagram host seam, `default-bind` by default;\n   * `:max-backlog`, `:repair-batch`, `:max-open`, `:repair-slots`,\n     `:repair-ticks`, `:repair-max-ticks`, `:max-repairing`: the\n     backlog and repair bounds (`defaults`).\n\n   Refuses an invalid option with its reason.  The node owns `:local`\n   from here: `close!` closes it.\"\n  [opts]\n  (let [opts (merge defaults {:bind! (default-bind)} opts)]\n    (when-some [why (option-refusal opts)]\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.space.dht/join: \" why)\n                      (dissoc opts :bind! :local))))\n    (let [local (local-store opts)]\n      (try\n        (node-over opts local)\n        (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n          ;; a directory join opened: release it, lock included\n          (when-not (:local opts) (jing/close! local))\n          (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn store\n  \"The node's `dao.jing` byte-store handle: put inserts into the local\n   store and records the address for the node's next publication,\n   answering the local verdict at once; get reads the local store; close\n   closes the socket and the local store.\"\n  [node]\n  (:handle node))\n         (if finalize (finalize opts extra) opts))))))\n\n\n(defn- release-store!\n  \"Release what a failed construction had already acquired: the\n   composition's transport state first (its boards, dials and socket), then\n   the store handle (a durable directory's exclusive lock), each exactly\n   once.  A cleanup never throws over the refusal that caused it, and never\n   replaces it.\"\n  [composition opened]\n  (let [close (:close! composition)\n        session (:session opened)]\n    (when (and close session)\n      (try (close session)\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n    (try ((or (:close-store! composition) store/close!)\n          (:index-store opened))\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(defn boot\n  \"Create the composition: one shell, one input medium, one cursor held only by\n   the step owner, and the host WebSocket adapter `(connect ...)` attaches\n   through.  A custody composition (:custody, yin.vm.ucf.compose) rides the\n   shell as data; the step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n\n   `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   past the engine's own two stores.  When it names the parsed\n   `:index-store-spec` as one of its own (`:composition-spec?`), `:open`\n   opens it and answers the two values of the ownership split: `:index-store`,\n   the generic `dao.jing` handle the engine is constructed with, and\n   `:session`, the transport state the composition keeps and steps beside\n   the engine — never inside it.  What the engine additionally needs to\n   drive that store arrives as `:engine-inputs` of the same answer (a\n   prepared `:link-source`, the composition's `:host-modules`), so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n\n   The engine value lands at `:repl`, where the driver and the endpoint\n   read it, and the composition's transport state at `:session`; there is\n   no third place a node could hide.  A construction that fails after the\n   store was opened releases what it acquired (`release-store!`) and\n   answers its own refusal.\n\n   `:admission` is the session's admission policy, by default `{}`: the\n   publisher key's own principal only.  It is apart from `:principals`: a\n   declared publisher is not a trusted one.\"\n  ([opts] (boot opts nil))\n  ([opts composition]\n   (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n         open (:open composition)\n         composition-spec? (:composition-spec? composition)\n         comp-store (when (and open composition-spec?\n                               (composition-spec? spec))\n                      (open spec opts))\n         repl-inputs (cond-> (if comp-store\n                               (merge {:index-store (:index-store comp-store)\n                                       :recovery (:recovery comp-store)\n                                       :publication-policy\n                                       (:publication-policy comp-store)}\n                                      (:engine-inputs comp-store))\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})\n                       true (assoc :publisher-key (:publisher-key opts)\n                                   :principals (:principals opts)\n                                   :admission (:admission opts {})\n                                   :custody (:custody opts))\n                       (:vm-type opts) (assoc :vm-type (:vm-type opts)))\n         state (try\n                 (driver/create-state\n                   {:host (or (:adapter opts) (host/websocket))\n                    :repl (repl.frontends/create-state repl-inputs)})\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                   (when comp-store (release-store! composition comp-store))\n                   (throw e)))]\n     (cond-> (assoc state :composition composition)\n       (:session comp-store) (assoc :session (:session comp-store))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition session\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn session-of\n  \"The composition session this host state carries: the engine at `:repl`\n   beside the transport state its composition owns at `:session`, joined as\n   the one value every composition function takes\n   (`yin.shell.session/make`'s shape).  Nil when the host drives no\n   composition.\n\n   The two halves live apart in the host state because the driver and the\n   served endpoint read the engine at `:repl` and know nothing of a\n   session, while the composition reads both.  A node is never inside the\n   engine value, so nothing engine-side can step one, and nothing\n   composition-side has to guess which key a session hides its node under.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [transport (:session state)]\n     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 1)\n     :cljs (.exit js/process 1)))\n\n\n(defn- custody-of\n  [state]\n  (get-in state [:repl :custody]))\n\n\n(defn close-index-store!\n  \"Release the composition's lifecycle resources before the host exits:\n   the custody composition's journals first (compose/close! -- the\n   authority and every journal backend the composition opened; it never\n   throws, so a failed close never blocks the exit), then whatever a\n   storage composition still owes, then the index store's own resources\n   (in durable mode, the exclusive directory lock).  The shell has already\n   stopped when a host calls this; the memory store has nothing to\n   release.  A composition's endpoints have been asked to stop and drained\n