foreign-bytes-set! p bv n)\n    n))\n\n;; ptr->string: NUL-terminated C string at ptr (NULL/0 -> nil)\n(define joltffi-ptr->string\n  (case-lambda\n    ((p) (joltffi-ptr->string* p #f))\nhost/gambit/source-loader-test.ss:16:(define (ce src) (jolt-pr-readable (jolt-eval-string src)))\nhost/chez/compile-eval.ss:923:(define (jolt-eval-string s . source)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"agent_message","text":"The vector failure comes from Gambit’s record tags. A plain vector starting with `16` can be mistaken for an RRB node, which sends a scalar into `vector-ref`. I’ll give record types distinct identity tags. I also found that the UDP cleanup path can call `close` before `O_NONBLOCK` is set, so the close rule needs stronger evidence than the descriptor flag."}}
