{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -12 build/p1f/first-eval.log; sed -n '932,950p' host/gambit/prelude-shims.ss; sed -n '312,340p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc; rg -n '\"'^('\"\\\\(define.*(gambit|source)|\\\\(define.*feature|\\\\(define.*conditional)' host/chez/reader.ss | tail -25; rg -n '\"'^('\"\\\\(ns|  \\\\(:require)' stdlib/jolt/{ffi.clj,socket/native.clj}; sed -n '715,750p' host/gambit/scheme-adapter-runtime.ss\"","aggregated_output":"(define (host-arity-like f wrapper) wrapper)\n;; A member-table write, which on Chez also moves the epoch its static-site caches\n;; validate against. Gambit's sites do not cache (host-statics.ss), so it is the write.\n(define (class-statics-member-set! h member v) (hashtable-set! h member v))\n\n;; Chez gensym accepts a STRING prefix; Gambit only a symbol. Normalize.\n(define %gambit-gensym gensym)\n(define (gensym . p)\n  (if (and (pair? p) (string? (car p)))\n      (%gambit-gensym (string->symbol (car p)))\n      (apply %gambit-gensym p)))\n\n(define-syntax fl=?\n  (syntax-rules () ((_ a ...) (fl= a ...))))\n;; The other R6RS flonum compares, for the cast fast path the back end emits\n;; on a proven double (fl>=? / fl<=? against the cast's window) and for the\n;; op registry's :dbl compares; Gambit spells them without the ?. These are\n;; PROCEDURES, not syntax like fl=? above: the emitted code reaches them\n;; through jolt-compile-eval's runtime eval, which cannot see a macro the\n(defn durable?\n  \"True when `store` is a durable directory store `open` answered (or a\n   handle composed over one, carrying its `:durable-dir`): its published\n   index outlives the process.\"\n  [store]\n  (some? (:durable-dir store)))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"Release a store's lifecycle resources — its content log handle and,\n   for a durable directory, the directory lock.  Nothing further can be read or\n   written through the handle afterwards.  Idempotent.\"\n  [store]\n  (when-let [close! (:close-fn store)]\n    (close!)))\n807:(define rdr-source-file (make-thread-parameter #f))\n876:(define rdr-kw-ref-source (keyword \"clojure.error\" \"source\"))\n877:(define rdr-kw-read-source (keyword #f \"read-source\"))\n1126:(define rdr-features '(\"jolt\" \"clj\" \"default\"))\n1134:(define rdr-read-features (make-thread-parameter '()))\n1136:(define (rdr-feature? kw)\n1140:(define rdr-reserved-features (list (keyword #f \"else\") (keyword #f \"none\")))\n2249:(define rdr-kw-features (keyword #f \"features\"))\nstdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj:17:(ns jolt.socket.native\nstdlib/jolt/socket/native.clj:34:  (:require [jolt.ffi :as ffi]\nstdlib/jolt/ffi.clj:1:(ns jolt.ffi\n    ((double) (joltffi-set-f64! addr off v))\n    ((float) (joltffi-set-f32! addr off v))\n    ((void*) (joltffi-set-u64! addr off v))\n    ((char) (joltffi-set-i8! addr off v))\n    (else\n     (error 'sa-foreign-set!\n            (string-append \"jolt.ffi: unsupported foreign type \"\n                           (if (symbol? type) (symbol->string type) (object->string type))\n                           \" on the gambit target\")))))\n\n;; bulk octet moves: ONE block copy foreign<->bytevector per call, the same\n;; shape the Chez adapter's memcpy path gives. The bytevector's body is\n;; borrowed for the duration of the synchronous call only (no collection can\n;; run inside it on this runtime); a count past the bytevector's end raises\n;; here, before the bridge dereferences anything.\n(define (sa-foreign-bytes-ref! addr bv n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref!)\n  (if (not (u8vector? bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy target must be a bytevector\"))\n  (if (or (not (exact-integer? n)) (< n 0) (> n (u8vector-length bv)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\" n))\n  (if (not (= 0 (joltffi-bytes-to-bv! bv addr n)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-ref! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n\n(define (sa-foreign-bytes-set! addr bv n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-bytes-set!)\n  (if (not (u8vector? bv))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy source must be a bytevector\"))\n  (if (or (not (exact-integer? n)) (< n 0) (> n (u8vector-length bv)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy count exceeds the bytevector\" n))\n  (if (not (= 0 (joltffi-bytes-from-bv! addr bv n)))\n      (error 'sa-foreign-bytes-set! \"jolt.ffi: bulk copy refused by the bridge\" n)))\n\n(define (sa-foreign-zero! addr n)\n  (joltffi-ensure-bridge! 'sa-foreign-zero!)\n  (joltffi-zero addr n))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
