{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'defn (payload-budget|announce\"'!|tick|step)'\"' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; sed -n '325,385p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '1310,1372p' /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc; sed -n '89,119p' host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-bridge.scm; head -45 host/gambit/ffi/joltffi-fixture.c\"","aggregated_output":"401:(defn payload-budget\n428:(defn announce!\n1422:(defn step\n   served endpoint read the engine at `:repl` and know nothing of a\n   session, while the composition reads both.  A node is never inside the\n   engine value, so nothing engine-side can step one, and nothing\n   composition-side has to guess which key a session hides its node under.\"\n  [state]\n  (when-some [transport (:session state)]\n    (assoc transport :engine (:repl state))))\n\n\n(defn with-session\n  \"The host state after one composition round: the engine back at `:repl`,\n   where the driver reads it, and the transport state carried beside it at\n   `:session`.\"\n  [state session]\n  (-> state\n      (assoc :repl (:engine session))\n      (assoc :session (dissoc session :engine))))\n\n\n(defn- composition-step\n  \"One transport step of the composition this host carries, at the host's\n   clock reading: `[state lines events]`, the events in the composition's\n   own vocabulary.  A host with no composition answers itself unchanged and\n   no events, so the engine's own tick path is the one that runs.\"\n  [state now]\n  (if-some [step (:step (:composition state))]\n    (if-some [session (session-of state)]\n      (let [[session' lines events] (step session now)]\n        [(with-session state session') lines events])\n      [state [] []])\n    [state [] []]))\n\n\n(defn- composition-recheck\n  \"One re-check of a parked run after this tick's transport events:\n   `[state text]`.\n\n   A composition drives its own re-check (`yin.shell.session`): it serves\n   the link and call media the engine parks on and translates its events\n   before they cross inward, so the engine re-checks only the generic\n   completions correlated to the work it parked and never decodes a\n   transport keyword.  A host with no composition calls the engine's own\n   tick re-check, which advances the one linker round the engine serves\n   itself and matches the same two generic event shapes.\"\n  [state events]\n  (if-some [recheck (:recheck-on-tick (:composition state))]\n    (if-some [session (session-of state)]\n      (let [[session' text] (recheck session events)]\n        [(with-session state session') text])\n      [state nil])\n    (let [[repl text] (shell/recheck-on-tick (:repl state) events)]\n      [(assoc state :repl repl) text])))\n\n\n(defn- composition-stop\n  \"Ask the composition's transport state to stop, once: its board server,\n   its dials and its socket are asked here and completed by `step`, and a\n   host never reaches past the composition to any of them.\"\n  [state]\n  (if-some [stop! (:stop! (:composition state))]\n    (if-some [session (session-of state)]\n                  :defect {:code ::walk-threw :text (or (ex-message e) (str\n                                                                         e))}}))\n        defect (when (map? v) (:defect v))]\n    (if (and (map? v)\n             (case (::walk v)\n               :missing (jing/segment-address? (:address v))\n               :complete (contains? v :value)\n               :invalid (and (map? defect) (keyword? (:code defect))\n                             (or (nil? (:address v)) (jing/segment-address?\n                                                       (:address v))))\n               false))\n      v\n      {::walk :invalid :address nil :defect {:code ::walk-shape}})))\n\n\n(defn- fail-load\n  [node m reason]\n  (let [{:keys [kind]} (get-in node [:loads m])]\n    [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :failed :reason reason\n                                              :fetching nil)\n                                     (dissoc :walk)))\n     [{::event :load-failed :manifest m :kind kind :reason reason}]]))\n\n\n(defn- advance-load\n  [node m done-by-id]\n  (let [{:keys [fetching kind walk], :as record} (get-in node [:loads m])\n        done (when fetching (get done-by-id (:id fetching)))]\n    (cond\n      (and fetching (nil? done)) [node []]\n\n      ;; the miss cause stays: another load may wait on the same address;\n      ;; advance-loads drops it once none does\n      (and done (not (:found? done)))\n      (let [a (:address fetching)]\n        (fail-load node m {::failure :miss :address a\n                           :cause (get-in node [:misses a] ::dht/gap)}))\n\n      :else\n      (let [fetched (cond-> (:fetched record) done inc)\n            node (update-in node [:loads m] assoc :fetching nil :fetched\n                            fetched)\n            walked (walk-outcome walk (local node))]\n        (case (::walk walked)\n          :complete\n          [(update-in node [:loads m] #(-> % (assoc :status :loaded :value\n                                                    (:value walked))\n                                           (dissoc :walk)))\n           [(cond-> {::event :loaded :manifest m :kind kind :fetched fetched}\n              (= index-kind kind) (assoc :datoms (count (:value walked))))]]\n\n          :invalid\n          (fail-load node m {::failure :invalid :address (:address walked)\n                             :defect (:defect walked)})\n\n          :missing\n          (let [a (:address walked)\n                {:keys [outcome id], :as asked} (content.step/request-get\n                                                  (:client node) a)]\n            (case outcome\n              (:requested :pending-request)\n              [(-> node\n                   (assoc :client (:state asked))\n{\n  ___SCMOBJ ___temp; /* the subtype test macros need a temp cell */\n  if (___HAS_TAG_AND_IS_NOT_DOUBLE (bv, ___tSUBTYPED, ___TB) && ___TESTSUBTYPE (bv, ___sU8VECTOR))\n    {\n      size_t len = ___U8VECTORSIZE (bv);\n      if (___CAST(unsigned long, len) < n)\n        return -1;\n      if (n > 0)\n        memcpy (___BODY_AS (bv, ___tU8VECTOR), ___CAST(void *, src), ___CAST(size_t, n));\n      return 0;\n    }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* bytevector -> foreign. Returns 0 ok, -1 bad count. */\nstatic int joltffi_c_bytes_from_bv (unsigned long dst, ___SCMOBJ bv, unsigned long n)\n{\n  ___SCMOBJ ___temp; /* the subtype test macros need a temp cell */\n  if (___HAS_TAG_AND_IS_NOT_DOUBLE (bv, ___tSUBTYPED, ___TB) && ___TESTSUBTYPE (bv, ___sU8VECTOR))\n    {\n      size_t len = ___U8VECTORSIZE (bv);\n      if (___CAST(unsigned long, len) < n)\n        return -1;\n      if (n > 0)\n        memcpy (___CAST(void *, dst), ___BODY_AS (bv, ___tU8VECTOR), ___CAST(size_t, n));\n      return 0;\n    }\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* read one int (4 bytes) from a caller-allocated errno cell */\n/* joltffi-fixture.c — the stage-1 gate fixture library (P1b-stage1).\n *\n * One extern \"C\" target per registered ordinary ABI shape the bridge carries\n * (p1b-inv/shim-registry.edn), plus the errno negative controls the repaired\n * W1-r2 pattern requires, and the errno-value probes so the assertions hold on\n * any OS. Built by the gambitffi* Makefile targets into\n * build/gambit-ffi/libjoltffi-fixture.dylib (and the two loader-smoke\n * libraries) with cc, loaded through jolt's own loader path.\n *\n * The TARGETS own their errno, exactly as W1's repair demands:\n *   - capture targets set errno themselves and return -1 (failure), or return\n *     a success value and PRESERVE the caller's errno (contract: do not\n *     normalize success to zero);\n *   - the intervening/post-capture clobbers are written AFTER the \"target\"\n *     portion of the call returns, so a shim that captures immediately defeats\n *     them, and one that does not is observable.\n *\n * Every symbol is exported with default visibility so dlsym sees it.\n */\n\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <sys/types.h>\n#include <stdarg.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#define JOLTFFI_CLOBBER 7777\n\n/* ---- errno probes (s01-shaped, so the gate reads them through the tier) ---- */\nint joltffi_fx_eagain (void) { return EAGAIN; }\nint joltffi_fx_eacces (void) { return EACCES; }\nint joltffi_fx_ebadf  (void) { return EBADF; }\nint joltffi_fx_eio    (void) { return EIO; }\nint joltffi_fx_eintr_c (void) { return EINTR; }\nint joltffi_fx_clobber_const (void) { return JOLTFFI_CLOBBER; }\n\n/* ---- ordinary shapes ------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n/* s01: () -> int */\nint joltffi_fx_layout_version (void) { return 42; }\n\n/* s01b: () -> int32 */\nint32_t joltffi_fx_eintr (void) { return (int32_t) EINTR; }\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
