    (try\n       (write-header! sa family len)\n       (set-sockaddr-port! sa port)\n       (if (= 1 (c-inet-pton family src (+ sa (if (= family af-inet6) 8 4))))\n         (do (when (and (= family af-inet6) scope-id)\n               (ffi/write sa :uint scope-id 24))\n             [sa len])\n         (do (ffi/free sa) nil))\n       (finally (ffi/free src))))))\n\n(defn alloc-sockaddr\n  \"A zeroed sockaddr_storage and its in/out length cell, as [sa lenp], ready for\n  accept, getsockname or getpeername. Reset the cell to sockaddr-storage-size\n  before reusing it. The caller frees both.\"\n  []\n  (let [sa (ffi/alloc sockaddr-storage-size)]\n    [sa (int-cell sockaddr-storage-size)]))\n\n(defn- named-address [f fd]\n  (let [[sa lenp] (alloc-sockaddr)]\n\n(defn message-bound\n  \"The effective transport message bound `node` composes under: the most\n   encoded bytes one DHT message carries.  Resolved once, at `join`, and\n   the same number the store front's oversize refusal uses, so a caller\n   that sizes anything against the transport reads the transport's own\n   answer instead of a default it guessed\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 5).\"\n  [node]\n  (:message-bound node))\n\n\n(defn payload-budget\n  \"The payload capability `node`'s transport declares: the most payload\n   bytes one `:store` message can carry inside `message-bound`, derived by\n   the transport's own encoder and envelope (`dao.jing.dht/payload-budget`)\n   and never hardcoded.\n\n   This is the number a storage composition over this node declares as its\n   generic `:max-payload-bytes`, so the bound the transport enforces, the\n   refusal the store front answers and the ceiling storage cuts pages\n   inside are one configuration's\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 5).\"\n  [node]\n  (dht/payload-budget (message-bound node)))\n\n\n(defn node-id\n  \"The node's id: 64 lowercase hex characters.\"\n  [node]\n  (get-in node [:composition ::dht/id]))\n\n\n(defn ack-peers\n  \"The distinct peers a blob must be handed to before it is `sent`.\"\n  [node]\n  (::dht/ack-peers (or (:dht node) dht/defaults)))\n\n\n(defn announce!\n  \"Declare that the blobs put through `store` since the last announcement\n   are the publication whose manifest is `manifest-address`: `step`\n   reports it `:published` once every blob has an outcome.\"\n  [node manifest-address]\n  (stream/append! (:ledger node) {::manifest manifest-address})\n  node)\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"Close the node's socket and its local store, discarding its ledgers\n   and queues unreported.  Idempotent; answers nil.\"\n  [node]\n  functions the marker exists for, where the caller's arity varies:\n\n      (defcfn c-open \\\"open\\\" [:string :int :&] :int)\n      (c-open path O_RDONLY)          ; empty tail\n      (c-open path flags 0644)        ; one-int tail, same binding\n\n  Three carriers decide the tail, as in babashka.ffi: an integer, pointer,\n  boolean or nil travels as a 64-bit integer; a floating-point number or ratio as\n  a double; a string as a NUL-terminated C string. Anything else raises at the\n  call rather than reaching C as whatever it happens to be.\n\n  A bare marker costs a compile on the FIRST call of each distinct shape — a\n  foreign-procedure's types are fixed when it is compiled, so a shape jolt has\n  not seen has to be built — and a cache lookup on every call after. Measured\n  end to end against a do-nothing C variadic, where a fixed binding is 20ns and\n  a declared tail 20.4ns: 26.5ns with no tail, 34ns with one value, 41.5ns with\n  two, and about 0.8ms once per shape. So roughly +13ns and 1.6x a declared\n  tail. Declare the tail where it is always the same; leave it bare where it is\n  not.\n\n  C's default argument promotions apply to a declared tail too: pass values\n  narrower than int as :int and float as :double, which includes :bool, since\n  _Bool promotes to int in a variadic call. Neither form combines with :blocking\n  (a varargs convention and __collect_safe cannot both be emitted), and the bare\n  form additionally takes no by-value aggregate — its tail is compiled at the\n  call, where an ftype the binding declared is not available.\"\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [with-open read]))\n\n;; The primitives this namespace is built over are the host's, reached by their\n;; reserved __ names: alloc, read, write, sizeof, string->ptr, copy, read-array,\n;; write-array, read-into!, read-bytes and write-bytes are all DEFINED here, over\n;; the host functions of the same name, so each needs a name its own definition\n;; has not taken.\n;;\n;; They are called rather than captured into locals. A jolt host with no FFI\n;; layer has none of them, and a top-level capture would then fail to LOAD this\n;; namespace instead of failing at the first foreign call — the difference\n;; between a host that cannot call C and a host that cannot read a jolt program.\n;; Inside a function body the reference resolves when it runs.\n\n;; -- layouts ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
